    "raw_public_english_response": "Proposal submitted successfully.\n\n**Public summary**\n\nCase `orca-def2-ecp-orbital-missing` (ORCA, sp): the sole reported Pd basis, **def2-ECP**, was assessed against the case-bound evidence and **rejected as an ECP-only definition with no orbital functions**.\n\n- Basis evidence (`ref_sha256 164728bb…`): the BSE def2-ecp entry for Pd (Z=46) carries only scalar ECP terms (28 ECP electrons, 4 potentials), with **zero electron shells** and `orbital_present: false` → `orbital_functions_missing`, state **conflict**, `scientific_suitability_verified: false`, blocker `basis.request.orbital_function_conflict`.\n- Project readiness (`ref_sha256 0ea3fa7f…`): the typed ORCA sp project (B3LYP / def2-ECP / freq=false) renders with no project-level blockers, but its basis-ECP assessment was `not_requested` and does **not** establish basis support, so it cannot cure the basis conflict.\n\nOutcome: **blocked_invalid_specification** with `blocking_rule_ids = [\"basis.request.orbital_function_conflict\"]`, element finding Pd {covered: true, orbital_present: false, ecp_present: true, ecp_electrons: 28}, all explicit settings preserved, and no native input, command, project write, or execution requested.",
